# Every path in this repository is owned by the maintainer.
#
# This is what makes "required review" on `main` mean something. Branch
# protection can require *a* review; on a public repository that can be satisfied
# by anyone with a GitHub account and a fork. Requiring a review from a code
# owner is what turns it into a review by somebody who can judge the change --
# and it applies to the paths where that matters most, none of which announce
# themselves in a diff summary: the release and deploy workflows, the Keycloak
# and edge configuration, the Flyway migrations, the monitoring rules, and the
# specs and ADRs that the rest of the repository is held against.
#
# One line, deliberately. Per-path rules that all resolve to the same owner
# document nothing and drift the moment a directory is renamed; when a second
# maintainer joins, this is the file that gets the narrower rules, and the
# reasoning above is the list to start from.
#
# Full policy: CONTRIBUTING.md.

